  "results": [
    {
      "id": "q_the_emergency_council_meeting_1",
      "question": "What are the wizards asking the council to do in the emergency meeting-and what's the catch?",
      "strict_verdict": "pass_updated",
      "semantic_verdict": "pass_updated",
      "must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown",
        "wards",
        "tradeoff"
      ],
      "semantic_must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown",
        "wards",
        "tradeoff"
      ],
      "context_must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown",
        "wards"
      ],
      "context_support_ratio": 0.5,
      "failure_surface": "pass",
      "stage_loss_tokens": {
        "wizards' college": "synthesis_gap",
        "arcane lockdown": "hit",
        "wards": "hit",
        "tradeoff": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The wizards are pushing for a citywide arcane lockdown to contain the threat\u2014but the catch is it will isolate parts of the city and potentially endanger or restrict civilians, especially anyone without proper protection.\n\nFrom the **CANON/OBSERVED city defenses and status**, there is a **\u201cProposed arcane lockdown\u201d** and a **\u201cPlanned magical lockdown\u201d** tied to the crisis (tainted meat/cult threat). The scale is large\u2014**\u201cEntire city is within purification scope\u201d**\u2014indicating the wizards want sweeping magical control over Mirathorn.\n\nThe catch comes from the consequences already noted:\n- **OBSERVED:** The city is **\u201cAt risk of having parts isolated if key tunnels or access points are sealed.\u201d**\n- **CANON:** Magical defenses and traps can discriminate (e.g., **amulet-based protection**, where those without them may be targeted).\n- **CANON/OBSERVED economy & atmosphere:** This risks disrupting the **festival-dependent economy** and worsening unrest (existing toll protests).\n\nSo the tradeoff is clear: strong containment vs. fragmentation of the city, civilian restriction, and potential collateral harm.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Proposed arcane lockdown; magical wards\n- Geography: Citywide scope; tunnels and access points\n- Economy: Festival-dependent; vulnerable to disruption\n- Operational Status: Crisis escalating; risk of isolation between districts",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_longmont_session_12_council_chamber_roster",
