        "wizard's college": "hit",
        "detect": "hit",
        "counter corruption": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright represents the wizards on the council, and he views the cult as a dangerous corruption of magic that must be detected and countered quickly with arcane means.\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright (the gnome head of the Wizard\u2019s College) is the council\u2019s arcane voice.  \nHis angle on the cult is strongly anti-corruption: he sees the tainted meat and related activity as \u201ca perversion of magic\u201d (CANON). This frames his response as both moral and technical.\n\nIn practice, he pushes for proactive magical solutions:\n- Deploying Wizard\u2019s College resources to detect and counteract the cult\u2019s influence (OBSERVED)\n- Using specialized detection magic (like a rune or spell) to identify corrupted meat (OBSERVED/CANON)\n- Supporting or initiating a magical lockdown of the city to contain the threat (OBSERVED)\n\nHe takes the threat very seriously and is eager to act quickly, though his inventive, tinkering nature can make him a bit distractible (CANON).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Head of the Wizard\u2019s College; arcane representative on the council  \n- Angle on Cult: Sees it as a perversion of magic; urgent threat  \n- Strategy: Magical detection, resource deployment, possible city lockdown  \n- Personality: Brilliant, inventive, but sometimes distracted",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
