      "answer": "TL;DR: There\u2019s no evidence Thalia is corrupted like the guards; what we have suggests something different\u2014likely influence or manipulation by the Wolf, not the same \u201coily sheen\u201d corruption.\n\nFrom the projection:\n\n- **Guards (OBSERVED)**: Corruption is clearly defined\u2014\u201cAll checked guards have an oily sheen to their eyes,\u201d along with mutations/merging behavior and mechanical benefits tied to corrupted meat. This is a consistent, physical corruption state.\n- **The Wolf (OBSERVED)**: Also shows signs of this corruption (\u201cWolf has an oily sheen to his eyes\u201d) and is explicitly a corrupting influence who \u201corders Thalia to attack the group.\u201d\n- **Thalia**: There are **no facts** stating she has the oily sheen, physical corruption, or shares the guards\u2019 condition.\n\nGiven that, the current, grounded interpretation is:\n- Thalia\u2019s behavior (attacking the group) is **caused by the Wolf\u2019s command/influence**, not confirmed shared corruption.\n- If she were corrupted in the same way as the guards, the projection would likely include the same \u201coily sheen\u201d indicator\u2014it does not.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Guards corruption marker: \u201coily sheen to their eyes\u201d (OBSERVED)\n- Wolf influence: orders Thalia to attack (OBSERVED)\n- Thalia corruption status: **not specified in projection** (no CANON or OBSERVED confirmation)\n\nIf you need a ruling at the table: treat Thalia as **controlled or coerced**, not fully corrupted\u2014unless new evidence emerges in play.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
