      "answer": "TL;DR: The council chamber fights back with arcane traps, illusions, and environmental hazards\u2014especially targeting anyone without amulets\u2014causing paralysis, force damage, disorientation, and falling debris.\n\nThe room itself is actively hostile:\n\n- CANON: Arcane defenses are keyed to amulets\u2014**Players (group)** without them \u201cmay be targeted by traps,\u201d while **Guards** are \u201cexempt\u2026via amulets.\u201d\n- OBSERVED: These traps manifest as **arcane trap bursts** that \u201ccan temporarily paralyze\u201d and deal \u201c2d6 force damage.\u201d\n- OBSERVED: The space is unstable\u2014players are \u201cforced to dodge falling debris hazards.\u201d\n- CANON/OBSERVED: Illusion effects are in play\u2014players are \u201cdisoriented by the illusory walls/illusion spells,\u201d compounding battlefield confusion.\n- OBSERVED: **Rune alarms** are active, escalating the fight by alerting enemies and locking things down.\n- CANON: The chamber ties into the city\u2019s machinery\u2014shifts in the **wall hum** can signal changes or trigger effects mid-fight.\n\nNet effect: the room punishes positioning, awareness, and gear (amulets), while scrambling player perception and layering damage + control effects.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Arcane traps keyed to amulets; rune alarms\n- Hazards: Falling debris; force-damage bursts; paralysis\n- Environmental Effects: Illusory walls; disorientation; shifting wall hum signals",
