      "answer": "TL;DR: Delay lets the cult advance their summoning via hidden routes while the city edges closer to disaster, with defenses unaddressed and internal instability worsening.\n\nIf the council keeps debating, the **cult (group)** continues operating unchecked through **hidden routes and sewers (CANON)**, advancing goals to **\u201caccess the heart of the city\u201d and \u201ccomplete their summoning\u201d (CANON)**. Their plans explicitly include **corrupting cauldrons** and using fallback paths if blocked, so inaction gives them time to adapt rather than stall.\n\nMeanwhile, the **city (location)** is already **\u201cbrought closer to disaster by each failed or unresolved debate\u201d (OBSERVED)**. Its **defenses have integrity concerns and less fortified areas (CANON)**, and a **planned magical lockdown (OBSERVED)** remains unrealized\u2014meaning vulnerabilities stay open.\n\nPolitically, **cult influence in the council (CANON)** raises the risk that delay isn\u2019t neutral\u2014it may actively favor the enemy. Social unrest (toll protests) and economic pressure (festival dependence) further destabilize things if no decision is made.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Threat: Cult summoning, sabotage, infiltration\n- City Status: Approaching disaster; unstable governance\n- Defenses: Known \u0915\u092e\u091c\u094b\u0930 points; lockdown not enacted\n- Political Risk: Council influence by cult factions",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
