      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room shows clear signs of a chaotic fight\u2014most notably the Wolf\u2019s corpse (decapitated; head removed from body) and multiple guards showing corruption with an oily sheen in their eyes, creating an atmosphere of tension and mistrust.\n\nWhat you should notice:\n\n- The Wolf (OBSERVED): His body is present and unmistakably defeated\u2014**Decapitated; head removed from body**. This is the clearest proof of the confrontation\u2019s outcome and his betrayal.\n- Guards (OBSERVED): Several guards display **an oily sheen to their eyes**, signaling corruption. Their behavior is tense and unstable, reinforcing that the threat isn\u2019t over.\n- Guard positioning (OBSERVED): Guards had been **placed in a ring along the wall**, suggesting a defensive or containment posture during the incident.\n- Atmosphere (OBSERVED): The guards are **visibly tense, some in disbelief**, indicating the fight has shaken confidence and control within the chamber.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition: Wolf decapitated; guards show oily-eyed corruption  \n- Defenses/State: Guards on alert, tense, and maintaining order  \n- Scene Tone: Aftermath of betrayal, confusion, and lingering internal threat",
