      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is **dead** at end of Session 12\u2014he was **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**\u2014and he had shown clear signs of corruption prior to death.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition (OBSERVED): **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**; previously had **\u201can oily sheen to his eyes.\u201d**\n- Operational Status (OBSERVED): Includes both escape attempts and \u201cescapes,\u201d but these are superseded by the terminal outcome.\n- Mental State (OBSERVED): Desperate, regretful, begging for release or death.\n- Loyalty/Alignment (OBSERVED): Cult-aligned; betrayed Mirathorn.\n\nResolution of Conflicts:\nThere is a conflict between earlier escape-related statuses (e.g., invisibility, fleeing) and the final condition. The **terminal outcome \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** takes precedence as the most current and definitive state. Bonogo\u2019s role explicitly includes **removing the Wolf\u2019s head**, reinforcing this outcome.\n\nFinal State:\n- Alive? No.\n- Corrupted? Yes, prior to death (oily sheen, cult influence).\n- Current condition: **Dead (decapitated).**",
