      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active, deceptive saboteur manipulating events; after, he is **\"Decapitated; head removed from body\"** and shifts into a desperate, regretful figure tied to the cult\u2019s corruption.\n\nBefore the fight (OBSERVED + CANON):\n- The Wolf is a **cultist** and **second-in-command of the guard**, actively undermining the council.\n- He uses **illusory duplicates** and deception to confuse both players and council members.\n- He is **strategic and evasive**, drinking an invisibility potion and attempting escape via a **secret tunnel**.\n- His role is a **confident manipulator and saboteur**, steering outcomes and ordering others (e.g., Thalia).\n\nAfter the fight (OBSERVED):\n- His state is terminal: **\"Decapitated; head removed from body\"**.\n- His **mental state shifts** to *desperate, regretful, begging for release or death*.\n- The detail **\u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d** reinforces his corruption and connection to the cult.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Saboteur \u2192 defeated enemy\n- Mental State: Calculating/deceptive \u2192 desperate/regretful\n- Physical Condition: Active/invisible \u2192 **\"Decapitated; head removed from body\"**\n- Tactics: Illusions and escape \u2192 no longer active (post-mortem state)\n\nNet: He goes from a hidden mover of events to a revealed, broken piece of the cult\u2019s influence.",
