      "answer": "TL;DR: The projection does not confirm Thalia was corrupted; the available evidence leans toward her being manipulated (\u201cplayed\u201d) by the Wolf, who is a cultist and actively deceiving others.\n\nThere is **no explicit fact** stating Thalia was corrupted (no mention of \u201coily sheen to the eyes\u201d or similar markers tied to corruption seen in Guards or the Wolf). By contrast, the Wolf **does** show corruption indicators (\u201cWolf has an oily sheen to his eyes\u201d) and is identified as a **cultist** actively sabotaging and deceiving.\n\nWhat we do know:\n- **OBSERVED:** \u201cthe Wolf orders Thalia to attack the group.\u201d\n- **OBSERVED:** The Wolf engages in deception, misdirection, and betrayal.\n- **CANON/OBSERVED pattern:** Corruption is consistently marked by physical signs (e.g., oily eyes), which are **not attributed to Thalia** in the provided context.\n\nThis suggests:\n- Thalia was likely **being manipulated or misled by the Wolf**, rather than knowingly acting under corruption.\n- The Wolf\u2019s role as a **cultist saboteur** ties directly to influencing others (like Thalia) to act on false beliefs or commands.\n\nIf Thalia were corrupted, the projection would likely include the same physical or behavioral markers seen in other corrupted entities\u2014but it does not.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- The Wolf: cultist; deceptive; \u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d; orders Thalia to attack\n- Thalia: (no corruption markers present in context)\n- Corruption pattern: consistently marked by visible traits (e.g., oily eyes) in other entities",
